From: Gemini PDA Linux bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] clk: name each clock clk_disable_unused() gates (#85 diagnostic)

TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC. Remove once the clock is identified.

#85's failing boot wedges inside clk_disable_unused(): the last thing it prints
is "clk: Disabling unused clocks" at t=1.009, then nothing at all for 23 s, then
a hard LOCKUP on two CPUs. On a healthy boot the next line arrives one
millisecond later. Gate a clock a block silently depends on and the next MMIO to
that block never completes, which is a hard lockup on whichever CPU touches it --
and the CPU pair does vary between failures, which is what made these records
look random.

This device has been here before. From configs/gemini-cmdline.config, 2026-07-04:
a kernel "went SILENT at exactly clk: Disabling unused clocks ... classic
incomplete-clock-tree hang". clk_ignore_unused was the workaround; the root cause
turned out to be 8250_mtk never enabling the UART's own baud clock, fixed
2026-07-06. There is evidently a second clock with the same problem, and unlike
the UART one it only bites some of the time.

So name them. The last name in the ramoops console record before the silence is
the clock that killed the boot.

The print sits inside clk_enable_lock() with interrupts off, which is safe for
printk but not free -- so this build also drops console=tty0 from the command
line. fbcon renders every line into a 1080x2160 framebuffer, and several hundred
lines of that would itself perturb the race this is trying to observe. ttyS0 has
no cable attached and the ramoops console zone is a memcpy, so neither costs
anything.

--- a/drivers/clk/clk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk.c
@@ -1405,6 +1405,15 @@
 	if (clk_core_is_enabled(core)) {
 		trace_clk_disable(core);
+		/*
+		 * #85 DIAGNOSTIC. The boot wedges somewhere in this sweep and
+		 * takes the console with it, so the name has to be printed
+		 * BEFORE the disable, not after: the last one in the ramoops
+		 * console record is the clock that did it. Remove with the
+		 * rest of this patch once it is named.
+		 */
+		pr_info("clk-unused: gating %s\n",
+			core->name ? core->name : "(unnamed)");
 		if (core->ops->disable_unused)
 			core->ops->disable_unused(core->hw);
 		else if (core->ops->disable)
